{"id":"1758d0f4-7f10-4d87-8f44-638cd128c0f7","object":"chat.completion","created":1785033485,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    # Validate minima sum and capacity sum\\n    sum_min = sum(s['minimum'] for s in segments)\\n    sum_cap = sum(s['capacity'] for s in segments)\\n    if budget < sum_min or budget > sum_cap:\\n        raise ValueError('Budget out of valid range')\\n    # Initialize allocations at minimum\\n    alloc = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\\n    remaining = budget - sum_min\\n    # Greedy allocation\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        best_score = -1.0\\n        for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\\n            if alloc[i] < seg['capacity']:\\n                # importance / (next position)\\n                score = seg['importance'] / (alloc[i] + 1.0)\\n                # break ties by earlier index (better score if larger, so we compare >)\\n                if score > best_score:\\n                    best_score = score\\n                    best_idx = i\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            # Should not happen if budget <= sum_cap, but break to avoid infinite loop\\n            break\\n        alloc[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    # Build by_name dict\\n    by_name = {}\\n    for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\\n        by_name[seg['name']] = alloc[i]\\n    total = sum(alloc)\\n    return {\\n        'allocations': alloc,\\n        'by_name': by_name,\\n        'total': total\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write a Python function solve(case) that implements the described algorithm. The case payload has: segments (list of dicts with name, importance, minimum, capacity), budget. The algorithm: allocate tokens to segments. Start with each segment at its minimum. Then while remaining budget > 0, pick t